  "description": "The 1894 bascule and suspension bridge as one structure: the two granite-and-Portland-stone Gothic towers on their river piers with corner turrets, hipped slate roofs and crowns, the two high-level lattice walkways, the bascules' lattice girders, the side spans' curved lattice chains with their hangers and medallions, and the shore abutment towers; pale blue and white paintwork, floodlit at night.",
